"type":"text"},{"text":"type. Slurs can add more elements using a continue type. This is typically used to specify the formatting of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cross-system slurs, or to specify the shape of very complex slurs.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSlur","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlslur","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSlur","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}],"title":"MXLNumberLevel","abstract":[{"text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSlur/number":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlslur\/number","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSlur\/number","title":"number","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier"